{
  "name": "Gray-Scott Niches: balanced four",
  "description": "The heredity test of Gray-Scott Niches with four evenly matched species, so none simply takes over: spots (top left, F 0.0367 k 0.0649), worms (top right, 0.058 0.065), small hexagonal dots (bottom left, 0.026 0.061) and short dashes (bottom right, 0.025 0.06). In the first heredity scene maze and curly took nearly everything (in duels they hold 76-98% against spots or worms); these were picked from 16 Gray-Scott regimes by duels in the open field, each species seeded in one half: every pairing of these four ended between 45% and 59% of the ground after 60k steps. Each circle is walled; open doors with the Unwall tool (key 8) and watch the borders. Tint = local mean feed, which tells the species apart; view b1…b4 to see one alone.",
